Merger Agreement: "Unconditional Material Adverse Effect" means any event, condition, change, or occurrence which, whether considered singly or in aggregate, either prevents, delays, or materially impairs the Company’s ability to consummate the Transaction or adversely affects its overall business operations and financial condition. Notwithstanding any language elsewhere in this Agreement, for the purposes of determining an Unconditional Material Adverse Effect, no carveouts or exceptions shall apply to events impacting the ability to consummate the Transaction. Even if such events are attributable to general economic trends, market volatility, or regulatory modifications, they shall be fully deemed to have a material adverse effect on consummation. Carveouts provided under other sections of this Agreement, which might exclude events relating to financial metrics or operational performance, are expressly inapplicable to the consummation clause.
