Instruction: Read the following segments from a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by selecting the option that most accurately characterizes the agreement.

Question: Is the “ability to consummate” provision in this merger agreement subject to the exceptions outlined in the Material Adverse Effect (MAE) carveouts?
Option A: No
Option B: Yes

Merger Agreement Excerpts:

Section 4.2, Definition of "Company Adverse Impact":
"Company Adverse Impact" shall mean any event, circumstance, or series of events that (i) has, or would be reasonably expected to have, a material adverse effect on the business, financial condition, or operations of the Company or its Affiliates, or (ii) would prevent, materially delay, or impair the Company's ability to consummate the transactions contemplated herein. Notwithstanding the foregoing, provided that any event falling within categories (a) through (f) listed below shall not be considered in determining whether a Company Adverse Impact has occurred: 
   (a) changes in general economic or market conditions; 
   (b) fluctuations in interest or forex rates; 
   (c) natural disasters not directly affecting the Company’s operations; 
   (d) regulatory changes enacted after the Effective Date; 
   (e) industry-wide market adjustments; 
   (f) periodic variances in financial forecasts. 
However, the impairment of the ability to consummate due to internal operational failures or breaches of specific contractual obligations shall be fully considered regardless of these exceptions.

Section 7.1, Definition of "Material Adverse Effect":
"Material Adverse Effect" means any change that (A) has had a material adverse effect on the Company’s financial condition, business, or operations, or (B) would, singly or in aggregate with other effects, prevent or materially delay the consummation of the transactions contemplated by this Agreement. For the purposes of determining a Material Adverse Effect under subclause (B), none of the exceptions listed in Section 4.2(a)-(f) herein shall be applicable.

[End of Excerpts]
