Instruction: Read the following excerpt from a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is the 'ability to consummate' concept exempt from the impact of Material Adverse Effect carveouts?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement Excerpt: 'Company Material Adverse Effect' means any change, event, or inaccuracy that (i) materially disrupts the Company's business operations or (ii) would reasonably be expected to prevent, substantially delay, or impair the consummation of the transactions contemplated by this Agreement; provided, however, that for the purposes of this definition, any changes or effects solely attributable to: (a) general economic fluctuations or market-wide shifts; (b) alterations in fiscal or regulatory conditions that do not cause a delay in consummation beyond 45 days; or (c) restructured commercial financing arrangements that have been pre-approved in writing by the Parties, shall be excluded from the determination of a Material Adverse Effect.\nEnd Excerpt.
